# Component reusability and clean Vue

Prefer existing shared building blocks. Extract a component when the same UI or logic appears more than once. Keep views thin: data fetching + composition, not one-off markup copies.

## Reuse first

- Check `src/components/shared/` (`ConfigField`, `ComponentTitle`, `ProfileCard`, `UiParentCard`, `CardHeader`, etc.) and `src/components/datatable/` before writing new UI.
- Follow existing config-driven patterns (page `config/*.ts` + `ConfigField`) instead of duplicating field/label markup.
- Put cross-page UI in `src/components/shared/`. Keep page-only pieces next to the view if they are not reused yet.

## Modular structure

- `<script setup lang="ts">`. One component, one responsibility.
- Props for data/config; emits for actions; slots for caller-specific content (`tableController`, headers, actions).
- Extract repeated template blocks into a child component, not a huge copy-pasted `v-card` in every view.
- Shared logic goes in composables or existing helpers (`@/utils/...`), not duplicated in each view.
- Avoid `any` when a small interface (like field config) is enough.

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD: duplicate card markup in every view -->
<v-card class="pa-3"><div class="text-caption">{{ label }}</div>{{ value }}</v-card>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: shared field + config -->
<ConfigField :config="field" :data="profile" />
```

## Clean code

- No unused props, imports, or empty `<style>` blocks.
- Name components by role (`ProfileCard`, not `Card2`).
- Keep templates readable: Vuetify layout classes on the component, not a wrapper `div` plus custom CSS.
- If a view grows large (multiple sections with distinct UI), split into colocated components under that feature folder rather than one 400-line SFC.
